ogles2.library licensing
========================

This repository holds code under two licences, plus third-party code that
keeps its own.

1. ogles2.library and everything built with PiStorm3D's V3D backend
   (ogles2/, v3dcore/, client/, cmd/, include/libraries, include/clib,
   tests/ except tests/corpus/, tools/builtin_shaders/) are under the
   Hyperion MiniGL Open Source License below, because v3dcore/ is
   PiStorm3D's backend (minigl.library 29.1, see v3dcore/PROVENANCE.md).
   In short: the library may only be built for AmigaOS, and the source of
   all modifications must be published to the Amiga developer community.

2. The parts that incorporate no MiniGL code are under the MIT License
   below: v3dp/, tools/v3dglslc/, tools/amictl/, tools/v3dp_tests/,
   tools/blake3_test/, tools/check_fpconv.py, gen/ (except gen/khronos/),
   tests/corpus/, dev/.

3. Third-party code keeps its own licence and notices:
   - include/GLES2/, include/KHR/: Khronos headers (MIT / Apache-2.0, see
     the file headers); gen/khronos/gl.xml: Apache-2.0.
   - v3dcore/: code by Macoy Madson and code derived from Mesa (Broadcom,
     VMware): licences/License_V3D_ThirdParty.txt.
   - ogles2/blake3.c follows the BLAKE3 reference implementation (CC0 /
     Apache-2.0); tools/v3dglslc builds Mesa (MIT) with the patches in
     tools/v3dglslc/patches.
   - The corpus programs (Mesa demos, the OpenGL ES 2.0 Programming Guide
     samples) are not in this repository: tests/corpus/build_corpus.sh
     fetches them.


